{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared"]]},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/JSONObjectEncodable","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/JSONValueDecodable","doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/JSONValueEncodable","doc:\/\/Readium\/SQ","doc:\/\/Readium\/SH"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DOMRange"}],"externalID":"s:13ReadiumShared8DOMRangeV","title":"DOMRange","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DOMRange"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"ReadiumShared"}]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Readium\/documentation\/ReadiumShared\/DOMRange","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"This construct enables a serializable representation of a DOM Range.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DOMRange"}],"platforms":["iOS"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In a DOM Range object, the startContainer + startOffset tuple represents the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"text":" boundary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"point. Similarly, the the endContainer + endOffset tuple represents the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end"},{"text":" boundary point.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"In both cases, the start\/endContainer property is a pointer to either a DOM text node, or a DOM","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element (this typically 